{title: 371 - Lift Him Up}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Eb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Christian Church}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[Eb]Lift Him up, 'tis He that [Ab/Eb]bids you, [Eb]Let the dying look and live;
[Eb]To [Ab/Eb]all weary, [Bb7]thirsting sinners, [Eb]Living waters will He [Bb/F]give;
[Bb/F]And though [Fm]once so meek [Bb]and lowly, Yet the [Bb7]Prince of heaven was He;
[Eb]And the blind, who grope in darkness, [Bb7]Through the blood of Christ shall [Eb]see.
[Eb]Lift Him up, the risen Savior, High amid the [Bb7]waiting [Eb]throng;
[Eb]Lift Him up, [Ab]'tis He that speaketh, Now [Eb]He bids you flee from [Bb]wrong.

Refrain:
[Bb]Lift Him up, the risen [Eb]Savior,
[Eb]High amid [Ab]the waiting throng;
[Eb]Lift Him up, 'tis He that speaketh,
[Eb/Bb]Now He [Bb7]bids you flee from [Eb]wrong.

Verse 2:
[Eb]Lift Him up, [Ab/Eb]this precious [Eb]Savior,
[Eb]Let [Ab/Eb]the [Bb7]multitude [Eb]behold;
[Eb]They [Ab/Eb]with [Eb]willing [Bb7]hearts [Eb]shall seek Him,
[Bb/F]He [Fm]will draw [Bb]them to [Bb7]His fold;
[Eb]They shall gather [Bb7]from the wayside,
[Eb]Hastening on with joyous [Bb7]feet,
[Eb]They shall bear the cross of Jesus,
[Eb]And shall [Ab]find salvation [Eb]sweet.

Verse 3:
[Eb]Lift Him up [Ab/Eb]in all [Eb]His glory,
[Eb]'Tis [Ab/Eb]the [Bb7]Son of [Eb]God on high;
[Eb]Lift [Ab/Eb]Him [Eb]up, [Bb7]His love [Eb]shall draw them,
[Bb/F]E'n [Fm]the careless [Bb7]shall draw nigh;
[Eb]Let them hear again [Bb7]the story
[Eb]Of the cross, the death of [Bb7]shame;
[Eb]And from tongue to tongue repeat [Bb7]it;
[Eb]Mighty [Ab]throngs shall [Eb]bless His name.

Verse 4:
[Eb]O then lift [Ab/Eb]Him up [Eb]in singing,
[Eb]Lift [Ab/Eb]the [Bb7]Savior [Eb]up in prayer;
[Eb]He, [Ab/Eb]the [Bb7]glorious [Eb]Redeemer,
[Bb/F]All [Fm]the sins [Bb]of men [Bb7]did bear;
[Eb]Yes, the young shall [Bb7]bow before Him,
[Eb]And the old their voices [Bb7]raise;
[Eb]All the deaf shall hear hosannah;
[Eb]And the [Ab]dumb shall [Eb]shout His praise.
